<title>UK: NWE straight-run fuel oil weaker with crude.</title>
<headline>NWE straight-run fuel oil weaker with crude.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE high sulphur straight-run fuel oil was steady to weaker on Friday alongside sagging crude futures, traders said.</p>
<p>Dealers said supply in Northwest Europe was limited and said today's confirmation that Russia would not repeat last winter's fuel export duty would not have an impact on prices.</p>
<p>Low sulphur fuel oil was steady to weaker with crude, with offers pegged at around $133 fob NWE.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
</text>
